---
// Privacy Policy – information according to Art. 13 GDPR.
// Describes ONLY what the website really does today. When a new feature collects data,
// add a section here BEFORE it goes live:
//   - newsletter service for sending (e.g. Brevo)
// The contact form (/contact) is covered under "Contact form" (added 26 Oct 2026).
// Field conditions on Home (Open-Meteo) is covered under "Weather on the Home page" (#weather,
// added 1 Nov 2026).
// Reserve (Netlify Forms + the confirmation email via a Netlify Function) is covered under
// "Reservations" (#reserve, added 28 Oct 2026) – the Reserve form links there.
// Favorites (localStorage, src/scripts/favorites.js) and the Pack (localStorage,
// src/scripts/pack-store.ts, added 28 Oct 2026) and the hidden coordinates (localStorage,
// src/scripts/coordinates.js, added 1 Nov 2026) are covered under "Data stored in your browser".
// Keep the newsletter purpose in sync with the note in Footer.astro.
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import EmailLinks from "../components/EmailLinks.astro";
import { owner } from "../data/owner.js";

const missing = (label: string) => `[${label} – to be added]`;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  lead="What happens with your data on this website – in plain words."
  description="Privacy Policy of the Cave Wear concept website."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No user accounts, no tracking, no analytics, no advertising.</li>
    <li>No cookies – that's why there is no cookie banner.</li>
    <li>Fonts and images come from this website's own server, not from Google or others.</li>
    <li>
      Data is only processed when you visit the site (technical server data), when the weather
      on the Home page loads (your IP address, and your rounded location only if you choose to
      share it), when you sign up for the newsletter (your email address), when you write to us
      (your message) and when you reserve your place (your first name, email and Pack).
    </li>
    <li>
      Favourites you save with the heart and what you put in your Pack stay in your own browser.
      Your Pack is only sent to us when you reserve it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>Responsible for data processing on this website (controller under the GDPR):</p>
  <address>
    {owner.name}<br />
    {owner.street || <span class="missing">{missing("Street and house number")}</span>}<br />
    {owner.postalCode || <span class="missing">{missing("Postcode")}</span>}
    {" "}{owner.city || <span class="missing">{missing("City")}</span>}<br />
    {owner.country}<br />
    Email:<br />
    <EmailLinks />
  </address>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted by Netlify, Inc., 101 2nd Street, San Francisco, CA 94105, USA. When you
    open a page, your browser automatically sends technical data to Netlify's servers: your IP
    address, date and time, the page you requested, the website you came from, and your browser
    and operating system. This is needed to deliver the website and to protect it against attacks.
    We do not use this data to analyse visitors.
  </p>
  <p>
    Legal basis: Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR – our legitimate interest in a secure and reliable website.
    Netlify processes the data on our behalf under a data processing agreement. Data may be
    transferred to the USA. Netlify states that it complies with the EU-U.S. Data Privacy
    Framework, for which the European Commission has issued an adequacy decision, and also uses
    the EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
  </p>

  <h2>Newsletter</h2>
  <p>
    If you sign up for the newsletter in the footer, we store your email address via Netlify Forms
    (Netlify, see "Hosting"). Netlify also records technical data of the sign-up – your IP address,
    your browser, the page you sent it from, and the date and time – and checks it automatically
    for spam. We only use your address to send you real news
    about Cave Wear – for example the launch, a vote on the next product or a big announcement.
  </p>
  <p>
    Legal basis: your consent, Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR. You can withdraw it at any time without giving
    a reason – a short email to the address above is enough. We then delete your address. Until
    then, we keep it as long as the newsletter exists.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact-form">Contact form and email</h2>
  <p>
    If you write to us with the form on the Contact page, we receive your name, your email
    address, the topic (and your own subject, if you choose "Other") and your message. The form
    is sent via Netlify Forms (Netlify, see "Hosting"), which stores it, records technical data –
    your IP address, your browser, the page you sent it from, and the date and time – and checks
    it automatically for spam. We only use your details to
    answer you – never for the newsletter or anything else.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our mailbox info@cavewear.de is hosted by netcup GmbH, Daimlerstraße 25, 76185 Karlsruhe,
    Germany, and forwarded to a Gmail account of Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow
    Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. We answer from there. The same applies when you email us directly.
    Google may transfer data to the USA; Google states that it complies with the EU-U.S. Data
    Privacy Framework.
  </p>
  <p>
    Legal basis: Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR – our legitimate interest in answering your request. If your
    message is about a reservation, Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR. We delete your message once your
    request is fully answered, unless the law requires us to keep it longer.
  </p>

  <h2 id="reserve">Reservations</h2>
  <p>
    When you reserve your place in the Pack, we receive your first name, your email address and
    what is in your Pack – products, sizes, fits, colours, quantities, for Supporter pieces what
    you chose to support, the Explorer's bonus if you added it, and the estimated total –
    together with the date and time. The reservation is sent via Netlify Forms (Netlify, see
    "Hosting"), which stores it, records technical data – your IP address, your browser, the page
    you sent it from, and the date and time – and checks it automatically for spam. Nothing is
    bought and no payment is taken.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use your details only for your reservation: to send you a confirmation email, to keep your
    place for the launch, and to write to you before the launch so you can confirm or change your
    order – never for the newsletter or anything else. The confirmation email is sent through a
    small Netlify function from reservations@cavewear.de, a sending-only address of our mailbox
    at netcup (see "Contact form and email"); replies to it reach info@cavewear.de.
  </p>
  <p>
    Legal basis: Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR – steps you ask for before a possible contract. We delete
    your reservation once the launch is over and your order is confirmed or declined – at the
    latest 12 months after you reserved. You can cancel it at any time by replying to the
    confirmation email or writing to us.
  </p>

  <h2 id="weather">Weather on the Home page</h2>
  <p>
    The weather on the Home page comes from Open-Meteo, a service of OpenMeteo GmbH, Hintere
    Schilligmatte 6, 6463 Bürglen, Switzerland. When this section comes near your screen, your
    browser asks Open-Meteo for the weather in Regensburg. Like every request on the internet, this
    sends your IP address and technical data about your browser to Open-Meteo. We don't receive or
    store any of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your location is only used if you click "Use my location" and allow it in your browser. It is
    rounded to about 11 km, and only this rounded position goes to Open-Meteo, directly from your
    browser. We don't receive it, and this website doesn't save it – not in your browser either.
  </p>
  <p>
    Open-Meteo states that it may collect IP addresses for server maintenance and to prevent
    misuse, that it doesn't link them to a person, and that it deletes its server logs, which can
    also contain coordinates, after 90 days. Its own{" "}
    <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/terms">terms and privacy notes</a> apply. OpenMeteo GmbH is
    based in Switzerland, for which the European Commission has issued an adequacy decision.
  </p>
  <p>
    Legal basis for the Regensburg weather: Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR – our legitimate interest in showing
    today's weather on the page. For your location: your consent, Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR. You can
    withdraw it at any time in your browser's settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Data stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    When you click the heart on a product, this website remembers your favourites in your browser
    (local storage) – only a short list of product names, e.g. "core-tee". It stays on your device
    and is never sent to us or anyone else. You can remove a favourite by clicking the heart again,
    or remove all of them by deleting this website's data in your browser settings. This is only
    stored because you asked for it (§ 25 (2) no. 2 TDDDG).
  </p>
  <p>
    When you add something to your Pack, this website remembers it in your browser (local
    storage) – only which product, size, fit, colour and how many, e.g. "core-tee, M, unisex,
    olive, 1". It stays on your device and is only sent to us when you reserve it (see
    "Reservations"). You can remove items in the Pack, or remove everything by deleting this
    website's data in your browser settings. This is only stored because you asked for it
    (§ 25 (2) no. 2 TDDDG).
  </p>
  <p>
    After you reserve, your browser also keeps a copy of your reservations – what you reserved and
    when, not your name or email – so you can still see them later. Deleting this website's data
    in your browser removes this copy, but it does not cancel the reservation itself.
  </p>
  <p>
    A few small coordinates are hidden on this website as a game. When you click one, your browser
    remembers which ones you found (local storage) – only short place names, e.g. "gjilan". It
    stays on your device and is never sent to us or anyone else. You can remove it by deleting this
    website's data in your browser settings. This is only stored after you click a coordinate,
    because the game can't work without it (§ 25 (2) no. 2 TDDDG). If you find all four and add the
    Explorer's bonus to your Pack, your browser also remembers that (local storage), so it can only
    be used once. It only says whether the bonus is unused, in your Pack or used.
  </p>
  <p>
    Netlify shows a small "Netlify" badge on
    the page. If you close it, your browser remembers this for 7 days (local storage), so the badge
    stays hidden. This is only stored because you asked for it (§ 25 (2) no. 2 TDDDG); it contains
    no personal data and is not used for tracking.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to social networks</h2>
  <p>
    Instagram, Threads and YouTube are linked as normal links – no buttons or feeds from these
    services are embedded. No data is sent to them while you are on this website. Only when you
    click a link do you go to their site, where their own privacy policies apply (Meta Platforms
    for Instagram and Threads, Google for YouTube).
  </p>

  <h2>Encryption</h2>
  <p>
    All pages are sent over an encrypted connection (HTTPS). You can see this by the lock icon in
    your browser's address bar.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>get information about the data we store about you (Art. 15),</li>
    <li>have wrong data corrected (Art. 16),</li>
    <li>have your data deleted (Art. 17),</li>
    <li>have the processing restricted (Art. 18),</li>
    <li>receive your data in a common format (Art. 20),</li>
    <li>object to processing based on our legitimate interest (Art. 21),</li>
    <li>withdraw a consent at any time, with effect for the future (Art. 7 (3)).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>A short email to the address above is enough.</p>
  <p>
    You can also complain to a data protection authority (Art. 77 GDPR). Responsible for us is the
    Bayerisches Landesamt für Datenschutzaufsicht, Postfach 1349, 91504 Ansbach, Germany –{" "}
    <a href="https://www.lda.bayern.de">lda.bayern.de</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>No automated decisions</h2>
  <p>We don't make automated decisions about you and don't create profiles.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When the website gets new features that process data, this Privacy Policy will be updated
    before they go live.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
